Ladybird treats nested object patterns as references into the assigned
value. Evaluating a computed key creates no object for the pattern,
and the destructuring expression returns the original assigned value.

V8 preserves the assigned value in a register while its bytecode
builder evaluates the computed key. BuildDestructuringObjectAssignment()
recursively calls BuildAssignment() for nested patterns, then reloads
the original value when the assignment result is needed.

JavaScriptCore evaluates a computed key with emitNodeForProperty() in
ObjectPatternNode::bindValue(), reads the assigned value with
emitGetByVal(), and recursively binds each nested target pattern.

SpiderMonkey evaluates keys in emitDestructuringOpsObject(), keeping
the assigned value on the stack. emitSetOrInitializeDestructuring()
recursively handles nested patterns through emitDestructuringOps(),
which leaves the original assigned value on the stack.
